<article class="env-example" id="02Z1">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/02Z1">Example <span data-tag="02Z1">65.14.1</span>.</a> Let $k$ be a field of characteristic $\not= 2$. Let $U = \mathbf{A}^1_ k$. Set </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  j : R = \Delta \amalg \Gamma \longrightarrow U \times _ k U  \]
</div>
  <p> where $\Delta = \{ (x, x) \mid x \in \mathbf{A}^1_ k\} $ and $\Gamma = \{ (x, -x) \mid x \in \mathbf{A}^1_ k, x \not= 0\} $. It is clear that $s, t : R \to U$ are étale, and hence $j$ is an étale equivalence relation. The quotient $X = U/R$ is an algebraic space by Theorem <a href="/tag/02WW" data-tag="02WW">65.10.5</a>. Since $R$ is quasi-compact we see that $X$ is quasi-separated. On the other hand, $X$ is not locally separated because the morphism $j$ is not an immersion. </p>
</article>